# Harmony AI App Active Context
@Focus:
- Sync Size-Estimate Confirmation + Toast-Suppression (2026-08-03): Cross-repo sync QoL work with harmony-link-private (engine). Three items:
  - (1) Engine size-estimate correctness (ENGINE repo): fixed the estimate/fetch mismatch — bare `strftime('%s', updated_at)` returned TEXT storage class so SQLite compared TEXT vs INTEGER watermark as "TEXT > any INTEGER" → every row counted (estimate said 7 records, fetch sent 0). Shared WHERE predicates `whereChangedSince`/`whereChangedSinceNoDeletedAt` in `database/sync_utils.go` now back all 32 `queryGetChanged*` fetch constants AND the counters (`CountChangedRecords` with internal table-name switch for 2-column `emotion_state` vs 3-column tables; `CountChangedCharacterImages` returns count+bytes). `sendSizeEstimate` covers all 33 tables incl. previously-missing `interactions`/`emotion_state`/`memories`; image-count query error no longer discarded. Verification: `go build ./...` + `go test ./database/ ./eventserver/` green (9/9 sync suite).
  - (2) Estimate confirmation protocol (ENGINE + APP): engine now BLOCKS after emitting `SYNC_DATA_SIZE_ESTIMATE` until the app replies with the new `SYNC_DATA_SIZE_ESTIMATE_CONFIRM` event (`{sync_session_id, event_id, status: SUCCESS|REJECTED}`), 60s timeout → engine sends `SYNC_REJECT` + aborts, NO data transmitted without confirmation. App-side: `SyncService.handleSizeEstimate`/`confirmSizeEstimate`/`pendingSizeEstimate` + new `sync:estimate`/`sync:estimate:confirm` events; `SyncConnectionContext` shows a themed dialog (Cancel→reject/Confirm→accept, `blockBackdropDismiss: true`) when the estimate exceeds the threshold or on initial sync. Empty estimates auto-confirm silently. Backward compatible (no estimate → sync proceeds as before).
  - (3) Toast suppression during expected handshake (APP): new pure gate `shouldShowConnectionErrorToast({isTransportSettled, isReconnecting, reconnectAttempt, isCertFlowActive})` in `syncSettlementHelper.ts` — never toasts on provisional/unsettled transports, during a cert-decision flow (cert modal is the intended UX), or inside the reconnect backoff loop (only the very first failure on a settled transport may toast). Wired into `SyncConnectionContext.handleSyncError` + `connect()` catch (new `isCertFlowActiveRef`, set on `cert:verification_failed` and before TLS dials, cleared on settled connect) and `ConnectionSetupScreen.handleConnectionError` (new `showCertModalRef` mirror). Kills the "connection error / connection dropped" toast spam during pairing when TLS/cert errors are expected. **Follow-up fix (on-device logs, adb logcat 08-03): a FOURTH ungated toast path remained — `ConnectionSetupScreen.handleHandshakeAccepted`'s catch showed "Failed to establish connection" whenever `attemptSecureConnection()` rethrew. Root cause: the failing connection is `InsecureSSLWebSocketConnection` (self-signed lib) which emits plain `'error'` (not `cert:verification_failed`), and `attemptSecureConnection`'s `isCertError` string check fails on the raw RN WS event (`{_defaultPrevented:false,_type:"error",...}` → no cert keywords) → rethrow → ungated toast. Log evidence: 08-02 builds toasted BOTH "Connection error occurred" AND "Failed to establish connection"; the 08-03 build suppressed the former (gate worked) but still fired the latter. Fixed by applying the SAME gate in that catch (`isCertFlowActive = showCertModalRef.current || !hasSelectedSecurityModeRef.current` — always true during pairing since `handleHandshakeAccepted` resets the ref to false → suppressed). New scenario test in `syncSettlementHelper.test.ts` pins the exact param set.
  - **Refactor (same session): the gate wiring was copy+pasted across the 4 call sites — extracted `shouldShowConnectionErrorToastForConnection` (async, dependency-injected: `getConnectionInfo` + `getSecurityMode` getters, so `syncSettlementHelper.ts` stays pure/unit-testable) in `syncSettlementHelper.ts`, which collapses the "resolve live settled transport via `isSyncTransportSettled` + run `shouldShowConnectionErrorToast`" block; new `SyncConnectionMode` type alias extracted from the inline union. All 4 sites (SyncConnectionContext handleSyncError + connect catch, ConnectionSetupScreen handleConnectionError + handleHandshakeAccepted catch) now call it. ALSO i18n'd the toasts: ConnectionSetupScreen had 11 hardcoded English strings — converted to `t('...')` (connection namespace; keys `connectionErrorToast`, `connectionCancelled`, `securityModeFailed`, `connectionRejectedToast`, `connectionFailedToast`, `reconnectedToast`, `reconnectFailedToast`, `unpairedToast`, `connectedToast` already existed; ADDED missing `failedToEstablishConnection` key). SyncConnectionContext already used `i18n.t('syncConnection:...')` — untouched. Verification: tsc clean; unit 28 suites / 333 tests (6 new for the async helper); integration 8 suites / 31 + 1 skip.
  - CRITICAL BUG CAUGHT IN REVIEW: the estimate payload field names. Engine serializes `SyncDataSizeEstimatePayload` with snake_case JSON tags (`estimated_download_mb`, `total_records`, `image_count`, `includes_images`, `image_size_mb`) but the app (and the mock server) read/wrote PascalCase (`TotalRecords`, `ImageCount`, `EstimatedDownloadMB`) — in production the estimate would always read as 0/0/0 and the dialog would NEVER appear. Fixed app reads + mock server emission + tests (Test 11 asserts `estimate.EstimatedDownloadMB` is `undefined`).
  - Themed dialog: reordered providers in `App.tsx` — `AppAlertProvider` now WRAPS `SyncConnectionProvider` (verified safe: AppAlertModal only depends on ThemeContext) so `useAppAlert()` works in SyncConnectionContext; replaced the RN `Alert.alert` fallback with the themed obsidian-glass dialog (icon `cloud-download-outline`, `blockBackdropDismiss: true`, Cancel→reject / Confirm→accept, `showAlertRef` mirror for the `[]`-deps listener).
  - Confirmation threshold: new pure helper `shouldPromptForSyncEstimate({totalRecords, imageCount, estimatedDownloadMB, limitMB, isInitialSync})` in `src/contexts/syncEstimateHelper.ts` — prompts ONLY when `estimated_download_mb > limit` (default 5 MB), `limitMB === null` = "Unlimited" → never prompt, empty (0/0) → auto-confirm, and `isInitialSync` → ALWAYS prompt for any non-empty estimate (bypasses limit). Initial sync detected via `ConnectionStateManager.getLastSync(getCurrentSource()) === 0` (no watermark yet — the watermark is only written at SYNC_FINALIZE). Setting persisted via `ConnectionStateManager.getSyncEstimateLimitMB()/setSyncEstimateLimitMB()/clearSyncEstimateLimitMB()` under AsyncStorage key `sync_estimate_limit_mb` (default 5, `'unlimited'` sentinel). `SyncSettingsScreen` gained a "Sync confirmation limit" dropdown card (1/5/10/20/50/100/Unlimited) via the shared `SelectPicker` + i18n keys (`estimateConfirmLimit`, `estimateConfirmLimitHint`, `unlimited`).
  - Verification: app `tsc --noEmit` clean; unit 28 suites / 333 tests green (13 syncEstimateHelper + 10 ConnectionStateManager + 6 connection-toast-helper new); integration sync suite 31 pass + 1 skip (syncService 14 incl. 4 estimate tests). Changes UNCOMMITTED — staged earlier sync-race work is still uncommitted too; user to decide commit split.
- Sync-Race Fix + Sync-Watermark Wipe Reset (2026-08-02): Diagnosed and fixed the "characters not appearing after pairing" sync failure; then added full-DB-wipe watermark reset and removed the legacy sync-timestamp alias. Three work items, all verified on-device + tests green:
  - (1) Settled-transport sync gate + abort safety net — root cause: auto-sync fired on the provisional plaintext ws:// pairing connection, then the ws→wss security upgrade tore the connection down mid-sync (buffered SYNC_DATA discarded, SYNC_COMPLETE dropped 4ms after listeners removed), orphaning `SyncService.currentSession` as 'in_progress' forever → every future sync logged "Sync already in progress, skipping" until app restart. Fixes: new pure helper `isSyncTransportSettled(connMode, persistedMode)` (`src/contexts/syncSettlementHelper.ts`) — TLS/cloud always settled, `unencrypted` only if user explicitly persisted it; `SyncConnectionContext.handleSyncConnected` is now async and defers `initiateSync()` until transport settles; new `SyncService.abortSync(reason)` (clears session/phase/buffer/serverRecordIds, rejects pending confirmation, emits `sync:aborted`) wired to `disconnected:sync` / `error:sync` / new `sync:connection_replaced` event (emitted by `ConnectionManager.createConnection` BEFORE tearing down an existing sync connection — the underlying WS 'disconnected' is suppressed there); Fix D: `handleSyncComplete` now `await sendLocalChangesSequentially(...)` so the phase machine advances deterministically; `SyncSettingsScreen` resets spinner on `sync:aborted`. Buffered server data is intentionally DISCARDED on abort (last-sync not advanced → engine re-sends everything = lossless recovery). Deliberately NOT reordered `disconnectConnection` (Fix C — CRITICAL blast radius, 25 callers/17 processes; documented follow-up). Tests: `syncSettlementHelper.test.ts` (9 unit), `sync.abort.test.ts` (3 integration w/ mock ConnectionManager emitting disconnected:sync/error:sync). On-device verification (emulator-5554, `ai.soulbits.chat.dev`): logcat shows gate "deferring sync until transport settles" (23:56:49.486) + "Aborting sync session: sync connection replaced" (23:56:49.649, 23:56:53.831); no stuck state; both sessions completed cleanly (0/0 because client DB was wiped but AsyncStorage lastSync survived — engine correctly had nothing newer; NOT a regression, expected incremental behavior).
  - (2) Full-DB-wipe resets sync watermark — root cause of "no data transferred after wipe": the app's SQLite wipe only removed the legacy `last_sync_timestamp` AsyncStorage key, while the per-source keys (`last_sync_timestamp:selfhosted`/`:cloud`) that `getLastSync()`/`setLastSync()` actually use survived → client told engine "synced up to <recent ts>" → engine returned 0 records. Fix: new `ConnectionStateManager.clearAllLastSyncTimestamps()` (removes all per-source keys) called from BOTH `wipeDatabaseCompletely` (Loading screen) and `clearDatabaseData` (Dev DB viewer). Per-source get/set, unpair/re-pair, app-restart persistence all untouched — only the full-wipe flows clear watermarks.
  - (3) Legacy sync-timestamp alias removed (Option B) — no long-lived installs from pre-per-source-migration, so dropped it entirely: `getLastSync` no longer falls back to `last_sync_timestamp`; `setLastSync` no longer dual-writes; `STORAGE_KEYS.LAST_SYNC_TIMESTAMP` deleted; `SettingsScreen` + `SyncSettingsScreen` "Last sync" display now read `ConnectionStateManager.getLastSync(getCurrentSource())`. Single source of truth = per-source keys only. Tests: `connectionStateManager.lastSyncReset.test.ts` rewritten (7 tests: per-source write/read, NO legacy fallback, wipe clears both, idempotent, credentials untouched); integration `syncService.integration.test.ts` + `sync.clock.test.ts` legacy-key seeds removed, `updates last sync timestamp on completion` now asserts legacy key is NOT written.
  - Verification: unit 26 suites / 295 tests green; integration 8 suites / 24 pass + 1 skip; `tsc --noEmit` clean; GitNexus detect_changes scope = wipe flows + settings screens' last-sync display only (risk HIGH inherent to destructive wipe flows). Changes UNCOMMITTED (4 sync-race files + 3 new files + wipe/legacy edits) — awaiting user decision on commit split.
- Google OAuth Environment Secret Wiring (2026-07-31): Dev/Prod OAuth client secrets are no longer hardcoded in tracked files. New `scripts/oauth-secrets.cjs` loader reads gitignored `client_secret_*.json` (search order: --file → secrets/<env>/ → secrets/ → repo root) and derives `.env` (APP_ENV/IS_BETA/GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID/APPLE_SERVICES_ID) + `android/gradle-secrets.<env>.properties`. npm scripts `oauth:dev`/`oauth:prod`; `android`/`ios`/`start`/E2E build scripts auto-load (with `--if-missing-ok` where optional). Android `build.gradle` resolves via -P flag → gradle-secrets file → '' (gradle.properties cleaned). Runtime: `cloud.ts` exports `APP_ENVIRONMENT` (env: dev|prod + label); `react-native-config.d.ts` typed `APP_ENV`; `googleSignIn.ts` warns when webClientId missing. CI unchanged (uses vars.* with -P priority; iOS regenerates .env per matrix entry incl. APP_ENV). `.env` untracked from git. Docs: `docs/OAUTH-SECRETS.md` + INSTALLATION.md update.
- Soulbits Cloud Config Convenience Features + Character Card Import (2026-07-30): Three user-requested features centered on the module config menu + Characters screen. (1) Endpoint auto-prefill: when Soulbits Cloud is the provider AND the app is cloud-connected, `ModuleConfigEditScreen.handleProviderSwitch` prefills `base_url` with the beta-aware `CLOUD_HOSTS.inference` (overrides the prod default baked into `PROVIDER_DEFAULTS.soulbitscloud.base_url`, which was the bug — beta builds showed the prod URL). Edit-mode never overwrites a stored value. (2) Module-filtered model dropdown: new `SoulbitsModelSelect` component replaces the free-text `model` field for soulbitscloud, loading valid models for the module type via a credential-less `createClient({inferenceURL})` against the public `GET /v1/models` catalog (5-min TTL cache, single-flight, never throws → static fallback on error/offline), plus a "Custom…" free-text override. Mapping in new `src/constants/soulbitsModels.ts`; service in new `src/services/cloud/soulbitsModelsCatalog.ts`. Shared infra: `FormField` `select` case now renders a real themed `SelectPicker` dropdown (was a disabled TextInput) — fixes existing select fields (reasoning_effort, aspect_ratio) too. (3) Character card import: ported harmony-link-private `utils/charactercard/` (types.go/png_parser.go/mapper.go) to a new pure-TS package `src/utils/charactercard/` (parser handles Tavern Card V1/V2/V3 from raw JSON + PNG-embedded tEXt/iTXt `chara`/`ccv3` chunks, base64-decodes; mapper → CharacterProfile + CharacterImage via `generateId()` UUID v7). Import service `src/services/CharacterCardImportService.ts` reads a picked file (RNFS), detects PNG/JSON, parses+maps+persists via existing repos (fully local, syncs via normal pipeline). CharactersScreen gained a header "Import Card" action (`@react-native-documents/picker` `pick`). Added `base64ToUint8Array` helper to `src/database/base64.ts`. i18n keys added to `moduleConfig.json` + `characters.json`. Tests: 6 new unit suites (jsonParser/pngParser/mapper/soulbitsModels/soulbitsModelsCatalog/base64) — 48 tests, full unit suite green (269 tests). tsc clean. NOTE: pre-existing eslint errors in ModuleConfigEditScreen (useCallback exhaustive-deps, unused moduleSpecificDefaults) + CharactersScreen (unused `Nav` type) are PRE-EXISTING (verified via git HEAD) — out of scope, left untouched. The `no-bitwise` warnings in the new binary-parsing code are inherent and don't fail CI. Manual/on-device verification deferred to user (build not run per workspace rules).
- Cloud-Mode Token Handling + Soulbits Model Defaults + TLS/UX fixes (2026-07-31): Six commits landed this session.
  - `353bf97 fix: Connection issue handling` — ConnectionSetupScreen cert-flow hardening: `hasSelectedSecurityModeRef` reset in `handleHandshakeAccepted`/`handleCredentialsCleared`/unpair/modal-abort; `handleCertVerificationFailed` → alert offering security-mode reset (i18n certResetTitle/Message/Confirm) then opens cert modal; "Reset Security Mode" button clears mode+resets UI+toast+opens cert popup; removed `setSecurityMode('secure')` dead-end. Root cause of phone TLS failure: app stores `harmony_server_cert` but never pins it; engine cert self-signed, SANs only localhost/127.0.0.1/::1 (no LAN IP) → "unknown certificate". Fix = re-pair in Insecure-SSL mode. Engine restarted with `SE_WSS_PORT=28443` (WSS/TLS); plain WS 28080, admin 28081.
  - `3167a8e feat: add speed dial button` — CharactersScreen FAB + modal replaced by RN-`Animated` speed dial: FAB rotates into ✕, two floating glass pills above it (Create Profile `testID=create-profile-option`, Import Character Card (PNG / JSON) `testID=import-character-card`), staggered open 220ms / close 180ms, backdrop/✕ closes; removed old modal + `createOrImport` i18n keys.
  - `7b3eb74 feat: simple profile picker` — CreateAIScreen links an EXISTING character profile instead of always creating a fresh one: profile selector + bottom sheet ("Create new profile" + all profiles); choosing one links the new entity to it (no unique constraint on `entities.character_profile_id` — verified valid), prefills Name/Personality, shows preview card with pencil → CharacterProfileEdit, hides photo/personality fields; alias conflict (`idx_entities_alias_unique`) → "Name already in use" alert instead of crash; `prefillProfileId` route param now honored.
  - `91fe902 fix: module pickers on create AI screen` — Advanced Settings: pickers were gated behind `hasAnyConfigs===true` (local-DB check) → empty DB showed dead-end "Connect to Harmony Link or Cloud…" warning. Deleted inline `ModuleConfigPicker` + warning block (~310 lines); 8 pickers now use shared `EntityModuleSelectorWithActions` (selector + ✎ edit + ＋ create → ModuleConfigEdit), always visible; `loadModuleConfigs` stable `useCallback`; `useFocusEffect` reload on return.
  - `5a10a51 fix: soulbits models defaults` — **no "soulchat" model exists on the live catalog** (`GET https://beta.api.soulbits.app/v1/models`, 20 models). Fake IDs removed: `soulchat-v1` (LLM fallback + `moduleDefaults.ts` default + `providerFieldSchemas.ts` placeholder), `soul-embed-v1`/`soul-tts-v1` (fallbacks), `whisper` (stt). Real replacements: LLM `qwen-35-9b`/`starfallen-24b`/`gemma4-meromero-26b-a4b`, embeddings `harrier-oss-v1-0-6b`/`qwen3-embed-4b`, TTS `harmonyspeech`/`kitten-tts-*`/`openvoice_*`/`chatterbox*`, STT `faster-whisper-tiny`/`faster-whisper-large-v3-turbo`, vision `qwen-35-9b`/`gemma4-meromero-26b-a4b`; default model `qwen-35-9b`. Added guard test: every fallback ID must exist in live catalog.
  - `5d5e7fe feat: convenience features for Cloud mode token handling` — see dedicated @Focus entry below.
- Cloud-Mode Token Handling design + implementation (2026-07-31): Engine (harmony-link-private) already injects the session PASETO into its seeded soulbitscloud row (`cmd/cloud_mode.go seedCloudSoulbitsCloudProvider`: seeds "Soulbits Cloud (default)" with `api_key=SE_INFERENCE_TOKEN`; `providers/soulbitscloud.go` switches PASETO-mode iff `api_key` starts with `v4.local.`). App-side gap closed: (a) **Inject on create** — `ModuleConfigEditScreen.saveProviderConfig` calls `injectSoulbitsToken({providerType, isCreate:!form.providerConfigId, providerConfig})` → sets `api_key` to current PASETO for NEW soulbitscloud configs only (updates/non-soulbits/standalone untouched); `handleProviderSwitch` also prefills `api_key` from `AuthService.getToken()`. (b) **Refresh propagation** — new `src/services/cloud/soulbitsTokenSync.ts`: `startSoulbitsTokenSync()` subscribes to `AuthService.on('auth:changed')` (login+register+refresh), bulk-updates all non-deleted soulbitscloud rows via new `updateAllSoulbitsCloudApiKeys(paseto)` repo fn (bumps `updated_at` so sync picks it up), THEN calls `SyncService.initiateSync()` to push to engine immediately (self-guards on in-progress/disconnected; connect-time auto-sync is the safety net). `syncCurrentToken()` one-shot on startup; `injectSoulbitsToken()` shared by UI. Wired in `AuthContext` useEffect (below DatabaseProvider → DB ready). (c) **Read-only credential UX** — `FormField` gained `readOnly?: boolean`: for password fields `editable={false}` + `secureTextEntry` locked + NO eye toggle + `contextMenuHidden`+`selectTextOnFocus={false}` (can't copy/reveal/break); soulbitscloud api_key rendered read-only when `isManagedSoulbitsApiKey` (same `v4.local.` prefix heuristic as engine). Tests: repo bulk-update (active rows updated, soft-deleted preserved), service (subscribe/unsubscribe, sync trigger, inject rules) — all green 279 tests/24 suites; tsc clean; GitNexus LOW on FormField (additive prop), medium detect_changes all internal to ModuleConfigEditScreen.
- Dev-mode detection audit + beta build commands (2026-07-31, informational): App knows dev via Metro `__DEV__` (compile-time) — gates logger severity, DatabaseTableViewer screen/menu/settings card, and `cloud.ts` `IS_BETA = __DEV__ ? true : Config?.IS_BETA`. FOOTGUN: exported `IS_DEV` alias = `IS_BETA` (beta-flavour), NOT `__DEV__`. soulbitscloud base_url prefill only when `cloudConnected` (mode==='cloud' && connected) — in dev connected to the local engine, creating a soulbitscloud config prefills PROD `api.soulbits.app`, while the model catalog (`soulbitsModelsCatalog.ts`) unconditionally hits `CLOUD_HOSTS.inference` (= beta in dev). Beta release build: `cd android; .\gradlew.bat assembleDevRelease -PE2E_DEBUG_SIGNING=true` (debug-signed, JS-bundled; only debug.keystore exists locally — no release keystore); output `android\app\build\outputs\apk\dev\release\app-dev-release.apk`; install `adb -s d608825c install -r <apk>`. `npm run android-prod` = prod flavor (IS_BETA=false) — NOT beta.
