@Decisions:
- Chat Message Types: Support 'text', 'audio', 'combined' (image support in progress).
- Audio Storage: Base64-encoded strings stored in TEXT columns (no BLOB/Uint8Array), transmitted directly via WebSocket.
- Audio Recording UI: Tap-to-start/stop (not hold-to-record) for better mobile UX.
- Dual Session Pattern: Each chat requires TWO entity sessions (user + partner) for separate event streams - critical architecture pattern.
- Multi-Connection Architecture: ConnectionManager handles multiple concurrent WebSocket connections with independent lifecycles.
- Device Pairing Flow: Handshake FIRST (unencrypted ws://) → user approval → upgrade to wss:// → cert validation → security mode selection.
- Security Modes: Three options (secure with validation, insecure-ssl without validation, unencrypted ws://).
- Heartbeat Protocol: Application-level CONNECTION_PING/PONG every 30s to maintain session.
- Real-time Indicators: Typing and recording indicators provide better UX.
- Optimistic UI: Store messages locally first, sync in background, handle conflicts.
- React Native CLI (not Expo) for full native module control.
- React Native Paper for Material Design 3 consistency.
- React Navigation for type-safe routing.
- TypeScript strict mode for type safety.
- Hooks -> Redux/Zustand as complexity grows.
- Dark theme default (matches Harmony Link, OLED-friendly).
- Database schema 100% compatible with Harmony Link for bidirectional sync.
- DEV-only test runner using __DEV__ checks for production safety.
- Logging: react-native-logs for all non-test code; console for test runners.
- InteractionSession Pattern: Replaces DualEntitySession; sessions scoped to interaction IDs (not partner entity pairs); events keyed by interactionId.
- Reply Mode: Per-chat-partner AsyncStorage preference; defaults to "realistic" (simulated typing delay), toggle to "instant".
- Emoji Action System: Entity-level emoji → action mappings persisted in DB (emoji_actions table), synced via WebSocket pipeline.
- Emoji Sets: Supports native (platform default), Twemoji (Twitter), and Noto (Google) sprite sheets via EmojiContext.
- Ekman8 Emotion Model: Emoji actions map to 8-base emotion deltas (joy, sadness, trust, disgust, fear, anger, surprise, anticipation), sent as additional_effects with messages.
@Decisions:
- Audio Duration Storage: audio_duration persisted to DB at message creation time (EntitySessionService for TTS messages) and on-load enrichment (ChatDetailScreen for historical messages). ChatBubble has zero DB writes.
- AudioPlayer Singleton Pattern: AudioPlayer is a singleton instance; static methods (e.g., getDurationFromBase64) must be called on the class itself (AudioPlayer as AudioPlayerClass), not the singleton default export.
- music-metadata v11: Replaces deprecated music-metadata-browser; works in Metro/RN bundler environments; parseBuffer(buffer, { mimeType }) returns format.duration in seconds.
@Decisions:
- CloudSessionStatus states: idle|requesting|provisioning|ready|failed. NO `active` service-level state — WS connectivity is tracked by useSyncConnection().isConnected. `canUseChat` (cloud→ready, self-hosted→isPaired) gates chat list and settings. `connectionStatus` produces mode-aware labels.
- BROKER_CONNECT_TIMEOUT_MS removed: the 30s client-side "force re-provision on stale ready" hack is superseded by the consecutive-WS-failure counter (5 → re-provision) and the broker's own lifecycle timers (connect-timeout arms at `ready`, abandoned-ready sweeper).
- Consecutive WS failure counter (MAX_WS_FAILURES_BEFORE_REPROVISION = 5): when RN WebSocket upgrades fail repeatedly without close codes, the app re-provisions the broker session instead of retrying against a dead session.
- Token-expiry pre-check before every cloud-mode WS dial: prevents expired-PASETO reconnect loops.
- Coupled release: backend + app deploy together. POST /connect response contract changes (409→202, 200-active→202-provisioning, failed→503). No API versioning; Beta project patches breaking changes through.
@Learnings:
- Wire-format-mismatch lesson: a payload consumer reading PascalCase keys against a snake_case JSON producer fails SILENTLY (all fields read as 0/undefined) — the feature looks broken-or-missing and mock servers that mirror the wrong casing hide it in tests. When an app reads engine payloads, verify the producer's actual JSON tags (Go `json:"..."` tags) FIRST, and assert the wrong-case key is `undefined` in tests to lock the contract.
- Blocking-confirmation pattern (engine side): the engine's sync handler can block on a confirmation channel (registered in `session.PendingConfirms` keyed by event_id) because `routeIncomingEvent` dispatches sync events on separate goroutines — same mechanism as `sendSyncDataWithConfirmation`. On REJECTED/timeout, send `SYNC_REJECT` + return error so `handleSyncStart` fails the session; never transmit data before approval.
- Initial-sync detection: the first sync on a fresh install is identifiable by `ConnectionStateManager.getLastSync(source) === 0` at estimate time — the watermark is only persisted at SYNC_FINALIZE, and `initiateSync` escalates to `force_full_sync` exactly when no watermark exists. This cleanly separates "initial sync" (always prompt) from an explicit user "Force Full Re-Sync" (watermark exists → threshold applies).
- Audio Playback Race Condition (Bug Fix): The `preloadAudio` useEffect in ChatBubble called `AudioPlayer.loadAudioForMessage()` on mount for every audio bubble simultaneously. Since AudioPlayer is a singleton wrapping a single TrackPlayer queue, concurrent `reset()` + `add()` calls from all bubbles corrupted each other's state – the last bubble's audio data was in TrackPlayer but `currentMessageId` might point to a different message. Fix: removed `preloadAudio` useEffect entirely; audio is only loaded when the user explicitly taps play.
- Audio Duration Enrichment Pattern: Duration is parsed from raw base64 audio using music-metadata (no TrackPlayer interaction). For new messages: EntitySessionService parses and persists immediately after creation. For historical messages: ChatDetailScreen runs a best-effort Promise.all enrichment on load; failures are silently swallowed (bubble shows '--:--').
- Static vs Instance in AudioPlayer: `export default new AudioPlayer()` is an instance. To call static methods, import the class separately: `import AudioPlayer, { AudioPlayer as AudioPlayerClass } from './AudioPlayer'` then call `AudioPlayerClass.getDurationFromBase64(...)`.
- Native Module Integration: react-native-audio-record and react-native-track-player require careful iOS/Android configuration.
- Runtime Permissions Critical: Always check/request permissions before accessing mic/storage; provide clear error recovery UI.
- Audio Recording Flow: Initialize → Check permissions → Start → Stop → Read file → Convert to base64 → Store as TEXT → Cleanup temp file.
- Audio UI Pattern: Tap-to-start/stop works better than hold-to-record on mobile (less accidental recordings).
- Base64 Storage: Audio/image data stored as base64 TEXT columns (not BLOB), simplifies handling and transmission.
- Database Migrations: Forward-only SQL migration files in /src/database/migrations/, numbered sequentially, applied automatically on app startup.
- React Native Track Player v5 Migration:
   - Android build fixed by upgrading to v5.0.0-alpha0 (Kotlin type safety fixes for React Native 0.83.1)
   - API changes: `getPlaybackState()` returns `PlaybackState` object (contains `state` property), use `getProgress()` instead of separate `getPosition()`/`getDuration()` calls
   - Update options: `notificationCapabilities` replaces `compactCapabilities`
   - State enum values are now strings (e.g., State.Playing = "playing")
- Base64 Storage Pattern: Audio/image data stored as base64 TEXT in SQLite for simpler handling and cross-platform compatibility.
- Chat UI Patterns: KeyboardAvoidingView essential for iOS, FlatList with inverted prop for message lists.
- Image Picker: react-native-image-picker provides good UX with caption support.
- Pulse Animation: Animated.loop with scale transform creates effective recording indicator.
- Typing Indicator: Three-dot staggered animation (150ms delay between dots) provides familiar UX.
- Metro bundler hot reload excellent with TypeScript.
- React Native Paper dark theme integration smooth.
- Migration from react-native-document-picker to @react-native-documents/picker fixed RN 0.83.1 compatibility.
- Gradle 8.13 required (NOT 9.0+) for RN 0.83.1.
- Database encryption with SQLCipher + React Native Keychain provides secure storage.
- In-app test runner provides better developer experience than Node-based tests.
- Base64 TEXT storage simplifies binary data handling compared to BLOB columns.
- __DEV__ checks ensure development tools invisible in production builds.
- ADB PATH setup critical for newcomers.
- Good foundation prevents technical debt.
- EventEmitter3 (~2KB) provides type-safe, reliable event handling for React Native (Node.js EventEmitter unreliable).
- TypeScript generics for EventEmitter interfaces enable compile-time event validation.
- Comprehensive logging with [ServiceName] prefix critical for debugging async WebSocket flows.
- Android emulator uses 10.0.2.2 to access host's localhost (not 127.0.0.1).
- Harmony Link must bind to 0.0.0.0 (not localhost) for emulator connectivity.
- HANDSHAKE_PENDING event handler essential for user feedback during device approval.
- ConnectionManager pattern enables multiple concurrent connections with independent lifecycles.
- Decoupling transport layer from service logic improves testability and scalability.
- Context separation (SyncConnectionContext vs EntitySessionContext) provides clear responsibility boundaries.
- React useRef critical for avoiding stale closures in setTimeout/async callbacks (reconnect counter).
- Reconnect race condition fix: Only schedule reconnect from disconnected event if NOT in isConnecting state.
- Event listener accumulation: Always call removeAllListeners() before disconnecting to prevent duplicates.
- Auto-reconnect strategy: Always retry regardless of error type, exponential backoff [1s, 2s, 4s, 8s, 16s, 30s].
- Logging transport enhancement: Custom transport to stringify Error objects (including stacks) prevents '[object Object]' logs.
- Dual Entity Sessions: Mirror Harmony Link's EntitySessionManager - each chat needs user entity session + partner entity session for bidirectional events.
- Device Pairing Sequence: Handshake happens FIRST over unencrypted ws://, THEN security mode is selected after cert validation on wss://.
- Connection Types: 'sync' for device sync, 'entity-{entityId}' for chat sessions - distinct connection lifecycle and event routing.
- Preset Sync Pattern: App does NOT use Harmony Link management API — all preset data flows through WebSocket sync pipeline. Preset name is plain text input, extra params edited as key-value pairs locally.
- Schema-Driven Config: App uses same providerFieldSchemas.ts as Harmony Link web frontend — ensures consistent provider configuration experience across platforms.
- Module-Specific Schemas Dead Code: UI looks up `PROVIDER_SCHEMAS[providerType]` by base provider ID — module-specific schema keys (e.g., `tts_openai`) were dead code. Module-specific fields merged into main provider schemas with tooltips.
- isProviderConfigInUse Pattern: Single UNION ALL across all module config tables is more reliable and maintainable than 8 separate existence checks.
- providers.ts Garble Prevention: When regenerating a file with many similar CRUD functions, verify all function signatures and table names match — agent can garble large files with repetitive patterns. 15 provider schemas, no module-specific schemas (one schema per provider across all modules).
- chat_template_kwargs Dropped: Both Go backend and app dropped this dead column in migration 021 — no longer needed for template customization.
- Model Field Unification: Migration 000030 consolidates `embedding_model`/`image_model`/`imagination_model` into single `model` column per provider config table. RAG structs keep `EmbeddingModel` domain name, mapper bridges.
- Generic Provider Mappers: One extract/load pair per provider in Go backend, not per module. Module-specific mapper variants deleted as dead code.
- Shared isProviderConfigInUse: Single UNION ALL query replacing 8 separate existence checks for provider config deletion safety.
- InteractionSession Migration: Refactored from DualEntitySession (keyed by partnerEntityId) to InteractionSession (keyed by interactionId). Events are now interaction-scoped, not entity-pair-scoped. Supports N participants per session.
- JOIN Query Performance: JOIN-based queries for chat list (conversation_messages JOIN interactions) reduced N+1 queries to single round-trip for last message preview.
- Session Resume Flow: INIT_ENTITY response now includes `resumed: true` flag; service checks if backend had a suspended session and reconciles state without re-creating connection.
- Reply Mode Implementation: ChatDetailScreen reads replyMode from active session; EntitySessionService sets it during INIT_ENTITY as `reply_mode` in session capabilities.
- Emoji Action Resolution: EmojiService scans outgoing message text for emoji characters, resolves against entity's emoji_actions table, produces AdditionalEffects payload sent with SEND_MESSAGE event.
- Reply Mode Default: Defaults to "realistic" if no preference stored; toggle persists per chat partner in AsyncStorage.
- Managed credential UX: never expose an injected server credential in a normal text field — render as locked read-only password (editable=false + secureTextEntry + no eye + contextMenuHidden) so it can't be copied/revealed/overwritten. `v4.local.` prefix is the reliable engine-side discriminator between PASETO-mode and plain API-key mode.
- DB-update-only ≠ engine-updated: a DB write alone is invisible to the engine until a sync happens — bump `updated_at` on bulk token refresh AND call `SyncService.initiateSync()` so the change propagates immediately; `initiateSync()` is safe to call unconditionally (self-guards in-progress/disconnected), and the connect-time auto-sync remains the safety net.
- Live-catalog-is-truth: hardcoded model ids (fallbacks/defaults/placeholders) must come from the real `GET /v1/models` catalog — fake ids like `soulchat-v1` were never shipped by the backend. Guard test (fallback ids ⊆ live catalog) prevents silent regression.
- PowerShell quirk: jest `--testPathPatterns` with `|` gets mangled by PowerShell piping — use `--runTestsByPath "a" "b"` instead.
- Cert-trust lesson: self-signed engine cert regenerated per boot with SANs only localhost/127.0.0.1/::1 will ALWAYS fail TLS verification against a LAN IP — re-pair in Insecure-SSL mode; full pinning/trust was deliberately not engineered.
- Sync-race lesson: auto-sync must NEVER fire on a provisional/transient transport. The pairing flow connects plaintext ws:// → handshake → wss:// upgrade; syncing on the provisional connection means the subsequent upgrade tears the connection down mid-session, discarding buffered SYNC_DATA and orphaning `SyncService.currentSession` as 'in_progress' forever (the "Sync already in progress, skipping" stuck-state bug). Gate auto-sync on transport settlement; add an abort-on-connection-loss hook as defense-in-depth so the state machine can always return to a clean slate.
- WS-teardown-suppresses-events lesson: `ConnectionManager.disconnectConnection` calls `removeAllListeners()` BEFORE `disconnect()`, so the underlying WS 'disconnected' event is never emitted on deliberate teardown — any mid-session cleanup must be triggered by a dedicated signal (e.g. `sync:connection_replaced`) emitted BEFORE the teardown, or it will silently drop.
- lastSync-lives-in-AsyncStorage lesson: wiping the SQLite DB does NOT reset the sync watermark (stored in AsyncStorage per-source). A wipe without watermark reset makes the next sync incremental against a recent timestamp — the engine has nothing newer to send, so nothing transfers ("no data during sync"). Any full-DB-wipe flow must also clear the per-source `last_sync_timestamp:*` keys.
- Incremental-sync-is-truth lesson: 0 records transferred during a clean sync is NOT necessarily a bug — if the client reports a recent `last_sync_timestamp` and the engine has no records updated after it, the engine correctly returns nothing. Diagnose by reading both sides: device logcat (SYNC_REQUEST payload `last_sync_timestamp`) + engine logs (`GetChanged* called with sinceTimestamp`).
@Implementation[Sync]:
- Multi-Connection Architecture: ConnectionManager manages multiple WebSocket connections (sync + entity sessions).
- Services[4]: ConnectionManager (transport pool), SyncService (protocol logic), EntitySessionService (session management), ConnectionStateManager (JWT lifecycle).
- Contexts[3]: SyncConnectionContext (sync connection state/actions), EntitySessionContext (interaction session management), EmojiContext (emoji style preferences).
- EventEmitter3: Type-safe pub/sub pattern, connection-specific event routing (event:sync, event:entity).
- Protocol: HANDSHAKE_REQUEST → PENDING → ACCEPT → WSS upgrade → SYNC_REQUEST → DATA exchange → COMPLETE → FINALIZE.
- Entity Sessions: Session resume on disconnect, dangling event reconciliation.
- Screens[2]: ConnectionSetupScreen (IP/port input, handshake), SyncSettingsScreen (status, manual sync, force full sync).
- Database: sync_devices, sync_history, chat_messages, interactions, emoji_actions tables. Migrations in /src/database/migrations/ folder.
- Error Handling: Connection validation, timeout handling (30s), confirmation tracking, comprehensive logging.
@Implementation[Chat]:
- Database: chat_messages table with TEXT columns for base64-encoded audio data. Migrations in /src/database/migrations/.
- Repository: chat_messages.ts with full CRUD, bidirectional queries, pagination, async transcription updates. JOIN-based interaction queries.
- Audio Services: AudioRecorder.ts (tap-based recording with permission checks), AudioPlayer.ts (playback controls).
- Voice Features: STT (Speech-to-Text) and TTS (Text-to-Speech) integrated and working.
- Native Modules: react-native-audio-record, react-native-track-player, react-native-fs, react-native-image-picker.
- Platform Setup: iOS (NSMicrophoneUsageDescription), Android (RECORD_AUDIO, READ/WRITE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE), runtime permission checks.
- Event Constants: TYPING_INDICATOR, RECORDING_INDICATOR, CONNECTION_PING, CONNECTION_PONG, STT_INPUT_AUDIO, STT_OUTPUT_TEXT.
- EntitySessionService: InteractionSession management (replaces DualSession), message sending (text/audio), STT async flow, heartbeat handling, reply mode support, session resume.
- UI Screens: ChatListScreen (entity selection, conversation list via JOIN), ChatDetailScreen (messaging with QoL: last message actions, new messages divider, auto-scroll, reply mode toggle).
- UI Components: ChatBubble (context menu for last message: delete/edit/regenerate, emoji-rich text), ChatInput (tap-based recording, permission recovery, emoji autocomplete), TypingIndicator, NewMessagesDivider.
- Navigation: ChatDetail route with impersonatedEntityId (roleplay support) and partnerEntityId/partnerCharacterId params.
- QoL Features: Last message actions, new messages tracking via ChatPreferencesService, mark-as-read on scroll, async transcription editing, reply mode toggle.
- Image Messages: Not fully implemented yet (placeholder support exists).
- Documentation: Complete integration guide in /docs/HARMONY-LINK-INTEGRATION.md with 5 detailed diagram files.
@Implementation[Interactions]:
- DB Migrations: 000024-000028 covering interactions table, drop session_id, interaction summary, memory lifecycle fields, presence_type.
- Model: Interaction interface (matches Harmony Link Go struct) with id, entity_id, scope, participant_key, participant_ids, status, presence_type, summary, memory_id, continued_interaction_id.
- Repository: interactions.ts with full CRUD (getInteractionById, createInteraction, updateInteraction), query by participant key, entity-scoped active interactions, getRecentPhoneInteractions, entityHasPhoneInteraction, getLastInteractionMessage (JOIN-based with TEXT column loading).
- Derivation Functions: deriveScopeFromParticipants (world/private/group), deriveParticipantKey (sorted pair/group join/empty for world).
- Sync Integration: SyncService syncs interactions via WebSocket pipeline; conversation_messages refactored to JOIN-based queries for chat list preview.
- Session Refactor: InteractionSession replaces DualEntitySession; events keyed by interactionId; supports N participants per session; navigation adapted.
@Implementation[Emoji]:
- Emoji Types: Ekman8Emotion (joy, sadness, trust, disgust, fear, anger, surprise, anticipation), EmotionEffect (emotion + signed delta), MetabolismVector, EmojiAction, AdditionalEffects, ResolvedMessageActions.
- Emoji Picker Components: EmojiPickerModal (full-screen with category tabs), EmojiPickerInline (compact for chat), EmojiGrid (virtualized grid), EmojiItem (single emoji with skin tone), EmojiSearchBar (keyword search), CategoryTabBar (swipeable category tabs), SkinToneSelector (5 skin tone modifiers), EmojiAutocomplete (inline text replacement).
- Emoji Display: EmojiAwareText (intelligent emoji/text segmentation), EmojiText (renders emoji in chat bubbles), ChatBubble custom rendering for emoji-rich messages.
- Emoji Services: EmojiService (data loading, search, skin tone variants), EmojiContext (style preferences, provider state management), EntityEmojiActionService (action CRUD + message resolution).
- Emoji Actions: EmojiActionEditorScreen (entity-level action management), EmojiActionCard (action list item), EmojiActionEditModal (action editor), CustomEmojiActionInput (custom action mapping).
- DB Migrations: 000022 (entity_emoji_actions table with emoji, action_type, emotion_effects JSON, style/bubble_color, cooldown_seconds), 000023 (deleted_at for soft deletes).
- Sync: emoji_actions synced via WebSocket pipeline, AdditionalEffects payload sent with SEND_MESSAGE events.
@Implementation[SamplingPresets]:
- App does NOT call Harmony Link management API for presets — only syncs via WebSocket
- Preset name is plain text input (user types name that exists on server)
- Extra params edited locally as key-value pairs (typical_p, tfs, dry_*, etc.)
- Precedence: explicit config > extraParams > preset values > library defaults
- DB: migration 021 added sampling_preset_name + extra_params TEXT columns to module config tables
- Provider config auto-created/updated during module config save via saveProviderConfig()
- Advanced Sampling Parameters component for OpenAI-family providers (openai, openaicompatible, openrouter)
- Provider field schemas in app mirror Harmony Link frontend (providerFieldSchemas.ts, moduleConfiguration.ts, moduleDefaults.ts)
- chat_template_kwargs column dropped from both Go backend and app (migration 021)
